Category: Signals & Systems 								
Difficulty: Medium 										
Points: 300

Description: We intercepted a deep-space RF transmission (muddy_signal.wav), but the sender's transmitter was incredibly weak. The signal is completely buried beneath the cosmic microwave background noise.
Fortunately, our recon team stole the baseband pulse template (template.wav) the transmitter uses before applying binary phase inversions to encode the 8-bit ASCII payload. The symbols are transmitted continuously 
with a fixed 50-millisecond quiet guard interval between them.

Task: Dig through the noise floor, demodulate the pulse sequence, and recover the flag.
